@page "/legal/acceptable-use"
<PageTitle>Acceptable Use — CrowdFund AI</PageTitle>
<div class="page-container py-5" style="max-width:800px;">
    <h1 class="fw-bold">Acceptable Use Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-muted">Last updated: 9 November 2026</p>
    <div class="cf-card">
        <p>You may not use CrowdFund AI to:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Fund illegal activity, violence, or sanctioned parties</li>
            <li>Misrepresent identity, purpose, or use of funds</li>
            <li>Upload malware, or attempt to bypass KYC/AML controls</li>
            <li>Harass others or post others’ personal data without rights</li>
            <li>Scrape, attack, or overload the service (including rate-limit abuse)</li>
            <li>Prompt-inject or manipulate AI systems to hide material risk</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We may remove content, freeze campaigns/payouts, and report to authorities.</p>
    </div>
</div>
